# CR 707.8a: a token created as a copy of a double-faced card not on the battlefield is a double-faced token, each face's
# characteristics those of the same face of the card as modified by the other copy effects - here Ardyn, the Usurper's
# "except it's a 5/5 black Demon". Ardyn copies Outland Liberator from Bot2's graveyard on turn 3; the token has daybound,
# so it becomes day (CR 702.145d). Bot2 casts nothing on turn 4, so turn 5 is night (CR 731.2) and the token transforms
# (CR 702.145c): Frenzied Trapbreaker, with nightbound, still a 5/5 black Demon - the exception applies to that face too.
# (Ardyn gives Demons menace, lifelink and haste.)
#
# Turn 1: Black Lotus and every Mox cast Ardyn ({5}{B}{B}{B}). Bot2 draws Outland Liberator on turn 2 and discards it to
# hand size; at Bot1's turn-3 beginning of combat Starscourge exiles it and makes the token.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Ardyn, the Usurper
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x7
Outland Liberator
Swamp x12

